<Programs>
<Program Name="MainProgram" TestEdits="false" MainRoutineName="MainRoutine" Disabled="false">
<Tags/>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="MainRoutine" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
All information provided  - No Warranty or implied merchantability. 
Refer to the RSLogix 5000 End User License Agreement (EULA) in the Release Notes.

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
Advanced Message Download

The next three rungs ensure the Advanced Message Download AOI is called only when there is a new message to display.  This AOI is used when one wants to create the messages in ladder rather than using InView Messaging Software and storing the messages in the InView.  New_message is the text you want to create - NOTE:  LIMIT YOUR TEXT/MESSAGE TO 50 CHARACTERS.  Dec_msg_number is the message number you wish to assign the new message.  If you don't want to store the messages on the InView, you can use a message number of 1.  The middle rung will convert the message number from decimal to hex as the full InView message string expects a hex value.  The AOI defines the rest of the message attributes from text position on the InView to color of the text.  Display_Address needs to be in hex as well - NOTE:  use a value of 00 for a broadcast.

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(New_message,Current_message)OTL(Adv_Trigger);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Adv_Trigger)Dec_to_Hex_Converter(InView5,Dec_msg_number,Hex_msg_number);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Adv_Trigger)[InVwAdv_Download(InView,Position,Mode,Justification,Font,Color,Flash,Hex_msg_number,New_message,Display_Address,Msg_Data,Dec_msg_number) ,COP(New_message,Current_message,1) ,OTU(Adv_Trigger) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
Alphanumeric Variable Update

The next two rungs ensure that the Alphanumeric variable update AOI is only called when the alphanumeric data has changed.  New_alpha_var_data would contain the alphanumeric data to display.  Alpha_var_number would be the variable number 0-99.  Display_Address2 would contain the specific display address (decimal format) to update if you did not want a broadcast update.  A value of 255 would result in a broadcast update.

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(New_alpha_var_data,Current_alpha_var_data)OTL(Alpha_Trigger);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Alpha_Trigger)[InView_Alpha_Var_Update(InView2,Alpha_var_number,New_alpha_var_data,Display_Address2,Var_Data) ,COP(New_alpha_var_data,Current_alpha_var_data,1) ,OTU(Alpha_Trigger) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
Message Triggering

The next two rungs ensure the message trigger AOI is only called if a new message is requested.  New_msg_number would contain the message number (decimal format) of the new message to display.  Display_Address2 would contain the address (decimal format) for the specific display if you did not want to broadcast trigger.  A value of 255 would result in a broadcast trigger.

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(New_msg_number,Current_msg_number)OTL(Msg_Trigger);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Msg_Trigger)[InView_Msg_Triggering(InView3,New_msg_number,Display_Address2,Msg_Data) ,MOV(New_msg_number,Current_msg_number) ,OTU(Msg_Trigger) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
Numeric Variable Update

The next two rungs ensure that the numeric variable update AOI is only called when the numeric data has changed.  New_var_data would contain the numeric data to display.  Var_number would be the variable number 0-99.  Display_Address2 would contain the specific display address (decimal format) to update if you did not want a broadcast update.  A value of 255 would result in a broadcast update.

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(New_var_data,Current_var_data)OTL(Var_Trigger);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Var_Trigger)[InView_Numeric_Var_Update(InView4,New_var_data,Var_number,Display_Address2,Var_Data) ,MOV(New_var_data,Current_var_data) ,OTU(Var_Trigger) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
</Programs>
